# Nothing in cron/ is a web endpoint. These scripts are run by the worker
# started in the Dockerfile, over the CLI, inside the container.
#
# They were reachable: GET /cron/process_notifications.php returned 200 from
# the open internet, so anyone could trigger a queue drain on demand. The lock
# file capped that at one run a minute, but a job runner that strangers can
# start is not something to leave open once it is sending email and SMS.
#
# Denying the directory rather than naming files, so a script added here later
# is closed by default instead of inheriting an exposure nobody remembers.
Require all denied
